<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fourth Anglo-Mysore War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1798–1799</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fourth Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a> War was fought in 1798–1799 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a> of Mysore and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>, allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizam-of-hyderabad">Nizam of Hyderabad</a>. Fearing a French alliance, Governor-General Richard Wellesley sent armies that stormed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srirangapatna">Srirangapatna</a> on 4 May 1799, where Tipu was killed. The British restored the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadiyar-dynasty">Wodeyar dynasty</a> to a reduced Mysore under their control.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fourth-anglo-mysore-war.jpg" alt="Fourth Anglo-Mysore War" width="320" height="257" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Henry Singleton · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henry_Singleton_-_The_Last_Effort_and_Fall_of_Tippoo_Sultan_-_WGA21457.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
